      "rationale": "Rhonchi and stridor are continuous adventitious sounds in both source taxonomies and map to ICBHI's Wheeze class; HF_Lung_V1's own paper pools W/S/R into CAS. That is the BROAD arm. The STRICT arm drops every row whose label depends on one of those two tokens, because ICBHI never annotated a low-pitched continuous sound or an upper-airway inspiratory one. Both are reported; the gap between them prices the judgement call."
